 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 326296,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The neighborhood of Pines West has three cul-de-sacs that meet at an intersection as shown. A postal delivery person starts at the intersection and visits each house in a cul-de-sac once, returns to the intersection, visits each house in the next cul-de-sac, and so on, returning to the intersection when finished. Describe how the route can be represented as a graph. If there is no backtracking, in other words, the person never reverses direction, is the route followed by the postal delivery person best described as a trail, an Euler circuit, a Hamilton cycle, or neither? Explain your reasoning.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b04f8fc6fd46f229.png\" alt=\"A map of Pines West. The map shows a start point at the center leading to three paths. Each path has six vertices. The start point is indicated by a vertex.\">\n",
